BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:event_316657277@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260924T115628Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261007T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261007T203000
SUMMARY:Lightning Talks
DESCRIPTION:The Boston Python User Group\nA presentation night with a hand
 ful of 10-minute lightning talks:\n\\- How It's Made: Python Packages — 
 Stephanie Goulet\n\\- Removing circular imports — Patricio Paez\n\\- Fra
 mework Comparison: Django\\\, FastAPI\\\, Flask — Kat Dobbins\n\\- Perfo
 rmance Still Matters — Mark Brown\n\\- LinkML\\\, unifying data structur
 e access — Vlad Korolev\n\nCome hear these diverse topics! Maybe they wi
 ll inspire you to begin work on one of your own. More about lightning talk
 s at https://about.bostonpython.com/lightning\n\nDoors will open at 6\, ta
 lks starting at 7. Plenty of time for hanging out and networking.\nPizza w
 ill be provided. We won't be able to record the presentations unfortunatel
 y.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/bostonpython/events/316657277/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260921T223558Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260921T223558Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
